      "message": "Hi Amara,\n\nThank you for considering jac-cloud for your Q4 infrastructure planning. To answer your questions:\n\n1. jac-cloud supports deployment on your own Kubernetes cluster, including managed services like AWS EKS. This is facilitated through our provided Helm chart, which simplifies installation and configuration. The runtime is containerized and stateless at the API layer, making it well suited for Kubernetes environments.\n\n2. Regarding horizontal scaling of walkers: jac-cloud\u000097s architecture allows you to manage replicas manually to ensure fine control over scaling. While the runtime is stateless and containerized, automatic horizontal scaling of walkers is not currently built into the platform, so you would typically configure Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler or other mechanisms to handle scaling as needed.\n\nPlease let me know if you need any further details or assistance with deployment.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]"
